275:\subsection{Replication check}
276:Before any seeding experiment we replicated each solver against its
277:published results on the twelve classical interval instances. The GA and
278:fEABC replications match the published average relative errors within
279:${\sim}1$ percentage point on all twelve instances (fEABC matches or
280:slightly improves on every one); fEABC-LS reproduces the published ranking
281:(best of its family). Our ABCE3 replication runs systematically
282:${\sim}1.5$--$2.5$ pp above the published averages; we were unable to close
283:this gap from the published description and disclose it here.
285:We take the published parameter settings verbatim, but that is a statement
286:about the configuration, not a claim that our implementation is
287:behaviourally identical to the authors' own. The ABCE3 gap above shows it
288:need not be, and the local-search footnote to Table~\ref{tab:portfolio} shows
289:where the two can diverge while the parameter file reads the same. Neither
290:affects any conclusion of this paper, because every seeding comparison is
291:within-solver: a seeded arm against the unseeded control of the same
292:implementation, under the same budget, on the same instances.
