The data files themselves are complete at eight arms: each `results_*.csv` has 14,640 observations (= 61 × 8 × 30), and each arm contributes 1,830 rows per solver. The inconsistency is therefore downstream/provenance, not missing runs. Several released “analysis complete” scripts still omit MIXH, including `audit_paper_numbers.R`, `fig_tables.R`, `rpd_vs_lb.R`, `compare_regimes.R`, and the default `auto_analysis.sh` pipeline; this matters because those scripts cannot reproduce the current eight-arm paper as released.
