SGS_IJSP_Append.h:31:/**
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:32:* An Append SGS is the simplest one. It schedules the tasks sequentailly
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:33:* following the given task order. Each task is scheduled immediately
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:34:* after its job and machine predecessors. 
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:35:* To do that, the algorithm will need to compute the maximum between the 
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:36:* completion time of those tasks, thus its behaviour may change depending
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:37:* on how that maximum is computed. This strategy is a parameter of the
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:38:* algorithm.
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:39:* In its simplest case, this SGS will produce semi-active schedules.
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:40:*
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:41:* @author hdiaz
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:42:*
SGS_IJSP_Append.h:43:*/
