The manuscript is unusually candid about the post-hoc arm and the TSN2 trace anomaly, which is a real strength. The problem is that the abstract and recommendations still outrun those caveats: “run to convergence” is asserted even though 111/244 control cells fail the manuscript’s own plateau rule, and the default-half recommendation relies on the exploratory arm.
